alex_lee: Heads-up — opened PR https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/7824 to add parsing examples covering some annoying edgecases for function/tool calling + a small link rewrite (old function-calling page -> /structured-output). Please review.

.docs-bot: PR #7824 opened by alex_lee — reviewers requested: @sophia @kevin

sophia: Can we include examples for: null vs empty array from tools, union fields (string|object), and a streaming fallback example? Real bug we hit: tools returning "result": null broke our parser.

kevin: I can update SDK snippets. Planning to add a TS example showing safe access + type narrowing and an async iterator for streaming responses. Any specific style preferences? (callback vs async/await)

melissa: Suggest a 'soft-fallback' pattern — prefer strict schema parsing but include a tolerant envelope parser that tries schema first then falls back to a best-effort parse. Example to include in PR:

```json
{
  "$id": "https://redwood.com/schemas/tool-result.json",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "tool_name": {"type": "string"},
    "result": {
      "oneOf": [
        {"type": "array", "items": {"type":"object"}},
        {"type": "null"},
        {"type": "string"}
      ]
    }
  },
  "required": ["tool_name"]
}
```

And show parsing pseudocode:

```js
// try strict parse
try {
  const parsed = JSON.parse(output);
  if (ajv.validate(schema, parsed)) return parsed;
} catch(e){}
// fallback: try to extract JSON-looking substring
const maybe = output.match(/\{[\s\S]*\}/);
if (maybe) return tryParse(maybe[0]);
// final fallback: return {raw: output}
```

alex_lee: Good pattern. Also noticed one doc link 404 — the old /function-calling/ reference needs to be rewritten to /structured-output/ and add a redirect. I'll include the link rewrite in the PR description.

chris: Small enterprise wording note — in the Private docs we avoid the term "guardrails"; prefer "validation checks". Can we add a parenthetical mapping in the top of the page so legal teams don't freak out? :grin:

sophia: I'll run the SDK smoke tests against the new examples. If they pass I'll stamp the PR. Any objections to modifying the python sample to use `response.get("tool_result") or []` instead of assuming a list?

kevin: pushed the TS changes and tests passed on CI — updated examples to use `response?.tool_result ?? []` and added a streaming iterator snippet.

melissa: small wording nit fixed in the PR: changed "If tool returns null" -> "If tool returns empty or null" and added an explicit example of `[]` vs `null` in the examples table.

alex_lee: Thanks — unless we hear objections I'll merge tomorrow morning and cut a docs patch. :thumbsup:

kevin: :thumbsup:

sophia: LGTM

